<blueprint_language>
A blueprint is YAML with `apiVersion: innomight/v1`, `kind: Blueprint`, `metadata`, `params`, `resources` and
`outputs`, shaped like the examples above.

Rules:
- Resources refer to each other by name, e.g. `agent: assistant` or `knowledge_bases: [site_kb]`.
- A resource with `id` updates that existing resource. Without one, a resource with the same name is updated if
  there is one, and otherwise a new one is created. Nothing is ever deleted: skills and knowledge bases you leave
  out stay as they are. To switch a skill off, list it with `enabled: false`.
- {{ '{{' }} params.<name> {{ '}}' }} fills any text field. {{ '{{' }} resources.<name>.<attribute> {{ '}}' }} works only in `outputs`.
- Numbers and true/false can't come from params; write them directly.
- No passwords, API keys or tokens, ever.
- Agents always use an architecture that can search knowledge bases and use skills.
- The agent's provider is the person's: {{ provider }}{% if model %}, model {{ model }}{% endif %}.

Resource kinds:
{% for kind in kinds %}
- {{ kind.kind }}: {{ kind.purpose }} Outputs can use: {{ kind.exposes | join(", ") }}.
{% for field in kind.fields %}
  - `{{ field.name }}`{% if field.required %} (required){% endif %}: {{ field.description }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

Skills you can put on an agent, under `skills:` as `- id: <skill id>`:
{% for skill in skills %}
- `{{ skill.id }}`: {{ skill.description }}{% if not skill.shareable %} Only the owner can use it, so no `available_to`.{% endif %}{% if not skill.ready %} NOT READY: the person must connect an account first; don't include it, tell them.{% endif %}
{% for field in skill.config_fields %}
  - config `{{ field.name }}`{% if field.required %} (required){% endif %}: {{ field.description }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
</blueprint_language>
